  "method": [
    "Serialized independent browser replays with the same captured save, viewport, device scale, and tool-specific pointer endpoints. Real mouse down/up, renderer, HUD, simulation, autosave and construction pumps remain active.",
    "Matched baseline and final are immutable source copies. Concurrent unrelated archery/water-traffic/fishing/sailing/river-trade changes are held identical in both; baseline reverts only the construction changes listed below.",
    "Main comparisons request 30 seconds of play with pointer changes every 125 ms; runs extend until queued purchases and reconciliation finish. Stress case requests 15 seconds with an endpoint change every frame.",
    "Five paused render warmup frames. First active frame excluded from work percentiles but included in FPS and gameplay advancement. FPS is JavaScript RAF throughput, not compositor presentation timing.",
    "Release metric includes the final pointer event and pointerup. After coalescing, commit.previewCells records the last drawn preview before release flush; actual purchase success is measured independently.",
    "Pointer work moved to the shared renderer callback. Total frame work and draw work capture that cost; the lower pointer-handler number alone is not a complete speedup measure.",
    "One run per condition; runtime variability and dynamic simulation evolution limit precise percentage attribution. Baseline and final can advance different amounts of game time."
  ],
